+- [ ] **Step 3: Define MySQL and Redis stateful services**
+
+Create `mysql.yaml` with a headless Service and one-replica StatefulSet named `moliapi-mysql`. Use
+`mysql:8.4.10`, database `api`, user `moliapi`, Secret keys `MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD` and `MYSQL_PASSWORD`, and arguments:
+
+```yaml
+args:
+    - --innodb-buffer-pool-size=80M
+    - --character-set-server=utf8mb4
+    - --collation-server=utf8mb4_0900_ai_ci
+    - --default-time-zone=+08:00
+```
+
+Add a `mysqladmin ping` startup probe, readiness probe, and liveness probe using the root password from the environment.
+Set requests to `cpu: 200m`, `memory: 512Mi`, limits to `cpu: "1"`, `memory: 1Gi`, and create a 10 Gi
+`ReadWriteOnce` volume claim template mounted at `/var/lib/mysql`. Set `runAsUser`, `runAsGroup`, and `fsGroup` to 999,
+disable privilege escalation, drop all capabilities, and use `RuntimeDefault` seccomp.
+
+Create `redis.yaml` with a ClusterIP Service and one-replica StatefulSet named `moliapi-redis`. Use
